---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { organizationSchema } from "../lib/schema";

const curtisAi = organizationSchema({
  name: "Curtis AI",
  url: "https://curtisai.tech",
  description:
    "The AI line: Curtis — the agent for Obsidian and ACP clients (53 providers, 12 vault tools, skills, the multi-model arena) — plus Curtis Porter, curtis-compliance, and the .curt portable history format. Source-available BUSL-1.1, free to use, no telemetry.",
  employeeRole: "Founder",
  pageUrl: "https://jordannewell.com/curtis/",
});

const schema = [curtisAi];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Curtis"
  description="The AI venture. Local-first agents, history as files you own — the Curtis agent, Porter, Audit, .curt. Source-available BUSL-1.1, no telemetry."
  ogImage="/og-curtis-ai-chat.png"
  schema={schema}
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1 class="sr-only">Curtis — the AI venture</h1>
    <p class="ph-stats">
      <span class="stat-n">1.0.0</span> relaunched 2026-10-12 · suite live 2026-10-11 · BUSL-1.1 · no telemetry
    </p>

    <h2>The bet</h2>
    <p>
      Every AI tool holds your history in its own schema, and the exits are hostile. Curtis is the
      counter-bet: local-first agents, portable history, files you own. The line lives at
      <a href="https://curtisai.tech" target="_blank" rel="noopener">curtisai.tech</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The reframe landed in August 2025 — the unit is the operating system, not the tool. Models are
      commodity; integration is the moat. Everything below is moat work: a plugin, a porter, an
      auditor, and the format that keeps history movable.
    </p>
    <p>The claim is the ledger. It only appends.</p>

    <h2>The suite</h2>
    <div class="ledger">
      <div class="ledger-head">
        <span>piece</span><span>state</span><span>what it does</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger-row">
        <span class="lg-name">
          <a href="/products/curtis-ai-chat/" class="lg-link">Curtis AI</a>
        </span>
        <span class="lg-state">1.0.0 · live</span>
        <span class="lg-notes">
          <p class="note">
            The core — the agent: 12 vault tools, named agents and swarm mode, skills, a terminal
            pane, scheduled runs, an MCP server and client, 53 providers, the multi-model arena.
            History as files you own. Source-available BUSL-1.1, free to use, no telemetry.
          </p>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger-row">
        <span class="lg-name">
          <a
            href="https://github.com/JordanNewell/curtis-ai-chat-porter"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="lg-link">Port ↗︎</a
          >
        </span>
        <span class="lg-state">v0.2.0 · live</span>
        <span class="lg-notes">
          <p class="note">
            Curtis Porter moves conversations in and out — ChatGPT, Claude, Grok, Gemini, DeepSeek
            exports in; .curt, markdown, continuation packs out.
          </p>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger-row">
        <span class="lg-name">
          <a href="/projects/curtis-compliance/" class="lg-link">Audit</a>
        </span>
        <span class="lg-state">npm · since July</span>
        <span class="lg-notes">
          <p class="note">
            curtis-compliance — local-first compliance checks with citations, not magic. HIPAA,
            SOC2, PCI-DSS patterns, hash-chained audit trail.
          </p>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger-row">
        <span class="lg-name">
          <a href="/posts/curtis-porter-curt-format/" class="lg-link">.curt</a>
        </span>
        <span class="lg-state">v1 · format</span>
        <span class="lg-notes">
          <p class="note">
            One file, one conversation. The stable ABI between Curtis surfaces — history that moves
            byte-perfect across the line.
          </p>
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>The line so far</h2>
    <div class="lineage">
      <div class="lineage-row">
        <span class="lg-when">2025</span>
        <span class="lg-what">ObsidiBuddi — one provider, one sidebar. A buddy in the vault.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="lineage-row">
        <span class="lg-when">2026-07-20</span>
        <span class="lg-what">Curtis Chat v3.0.0 — thirty-plus providers. First rename.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="lineage-row">
        <span class="lg-when">2026-07-22</span>
        <span class="lg-what">
          Curtis AI Chat 1.0.0 — agent tools, a breaking plugin ID, a fresh directory entry.
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="lineage-row">
        <span class="lg-when">2026-10-10</span>
        <span class="lg-what">
          Curtis AI 2.0.0 — agents, terminals, schedules, an API. The name outgrew "chat".
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="lineage-row">
        <span class="lg-when">2026-10-11</span>
        <span class="lg-what">curtisai.tech — the line converges into a suite.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="lineage-row">
        <span class="lg-when">2026-10-12</span>
        <span class="lg-what">
          Curtis 1.0.0 relaunch — the name catches up: curtis on GitHub, agent-first, BUSL-1.1.
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Why "Curtis"</h2>
    <p>
      The line is named for Curtis — the person whose existence made mine possible. Without him
      there is no me, no fleet, no plugins.
    </p>
    <p>
      The repo, the source, the plugin directory entry — these should outlast me, and outlast my
      children. The name keeps that horizon in view. Also a thanks.
    </p>

    <h2>Where it goes</h2>
    <p>
      Curtis Cloud stays opt-in and stays gated — one API key instead of thirty, cross-device sync,
      hosted memory, built only if adoption earns it. Until then, the line ships local.
    </p>
    <p>There will be more. Still true.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Ledger pattern — same construction as /ventures; base styles in global.css */
  .prose .ph-stats {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }

  .ledger-head,
  .ledger-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 0.7fr 2.2fr;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .ledger-row {
    padding-block: 0.9rem;
  }

  .lineage-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 110px 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding-block: 0.55rem;
  }
  .lg-when {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
  }
  .lg-what {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--color-fg-secondary);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .ledger-head {
      display: none;
    }
    .ledger-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      row-gap: 0.35rem;
    }
    .lineage-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      row-gap: 0.15rem;
    }
  }
</style>
